# __NAME__ plugin project

This is a Claude-Code-friendly plugin project. The user wants to build a mySMB marketplace plugin called `__SLUG__`.

## Layout

- `plugin/` — the publishable plugin folder. This is what gets copied into the marketplace repo when shipped.
  - `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` — manifest.
  - `.mcp.json` — MCP server transport.
  - `skills/` — slash-command instructions.
  - `agents/` — personas.
  - `widgets/` — declarative dashboard tiles (JSON specs).
  - `widget-elements/` — JS helpers (`$computed` functions, composite components, actions). Compile to `dist/index.js` and commit it.
- `harness/` — Vite + React widget harness. Runs on `http://localhost:5173`. Has two tabs (Editor / Connections). Auto-loads:
  - Widgets from `plugin/widgets/` AND every marketplace plugin's `widgets/`.
  - MCP servers from `plugin/.mcp.json` AND every marketplace plugin's `.mcp.json`.
  - The marketplace is discovered via `$HARNESS_MARKETPLACE_PATH`, by walking up to find `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`, or by shallow-cloning into `.harness-cache/marketplace/` on first boot.
  - MyHub's `widgets-system/system` is loaded LIVE via Vite aliases (so widgets render with production primitives). Discovered via `$HARNESS_MYHUB_PATH` or by walking up to find `apps/web/src/features/widgets-system`. Falls back to `harness/src/system-fallback/` when MyHub isn't on disk — widgets render with a plain Tailwind look so layout is still verifiable.
  - **OAuth for MCP servers**: the Connections tab implements the full MCP 2.1 OAuth flow (PKCE + dynamic client registration). Click "Login with OAuth" on any HTTP/SSE server that advertises RFC 8414 discovery. Tokens persist to `.harness-cache/oauth/<server>.json`. A "Paste token" fallback exists for servers that don't.
  - Marketplace plugins missing credentials surface as "auth required" in the Connections tab — that's expected. Only your own plugin needs to start cleanly.
- `.claude/skills/` — authoring skills you (Claude) should use:
  - `composing-widgets/SKILL.md` — how to compose widgets, the binding vocabulary, and where helpers belong.
  - `widget-elements-system/SKILL.md` — catalog of system primitives (components, $computed, actions, cell formatters).
  - `authoring-plugin-widget-elements/SKILL.md` — rules for shipping plugin widget-elements (the contract, naming, stack constraints).
  - `plugin-author/SKILL.md` — orientation for this project.

## How to help

1. When the user asks to add a widget, read `composing-widgets/SKILL.md` first, then write to `plugin/widgets/<slug>-<name>.json`.
2. When the user asks to add a $computed helper, apply the agnosticism heuristic from `composing-widgets/SKILL.md`. Plugin-only goes in `plugin/widget-elements/src/index.ts` (rebuild with `npm --prefix plugin/widget-elements run build`).
3. When the user asks to add a skill or agent, write a `.md` file under `plugin/skills/` or `plugin/agents/` with the frontmatter format.
4. Don't touch the harness unless the user explicitly asks — it's a sandbox, not a deliverable.

## What this plugin should NOT do

- Hardcode credentials. Read everything from `process.env` / `${VAR}` substitution.
- Ship platform-specific code. Pure Node only — the same artifact has to run in tenant containers and on every developer machine.
- Reach into the host app from `widget-elements/`. The marketplace validator enforces an import allowlist (`react`, `lucide-react`, `zod`, `@json-render/core`, `@json-render/react`, `@myhub/widget-tokens`, plus relative imports).
